Babet current roadmap (2.23.0 release)
=====================================

Legend: [ ] todo, [~] in progress/pending validation, [x] completed.
The ZIP supplied for each work session is the primary source of truth for
files to modify. GitHub is a complementary reference and must not silently
override a different local ZIP state.

Release hardening — fixed-width public ABI tags
------------------------------------------------

[x] Reproduce the 2.23.0 pre-release UBSan failure caused by loading the invalid
    numeric `babet_value.type` fixture through a C++ enum object before validation.
[x] Make `babet_status` and `babet_value_type` fixed-width `uint32_t` ABI tags so
    unknown numeric values remain representable and can be rejected explicitly.
[x] Extend the C embedding smoke with compile-time width assertions and an
    invalid host callback status, covering both public discriminants.
[x] Re-run the complete `./run_tests.sh --release` maintainer campaign after the
    fixed-width ABI-tag correction. ASan/UBSan embedding reaches 10/0, the
    restored normal embedding campaign reaches 16/0, the complete normal
    harness remains 3810/0 folder, 3796/0 embedded, 3796/0 embedded-via-PATH
    and 9/9 modes, while network smoke tests reach 11 PASS / 0 FAIL / 0 WARN.

