Lot 1 — quick measurement of the current release binary
--------------------------------------------------------

[x] Measure the actual distributed stripped x86_64 release binary with:
    stat -c '%s' babet; file babet; ldd babet; size -A babet.
[x] Confirm release stripping is effective: the v2.22.2 published binary is
    reported as stripped and contains no .debug_* or .zdebug_* sections.
[x] Confirm stripping directly with
    `readelf -S | grep -E '\.symtab|\.strtab'` on the published binary: the
    release contains neither `.symtab` nor `.strtab`.
[x] Check dynamic dependencies: only libc, libm and the ELF loader are dynamic;
    no accidentally externalised Babet dependency appears in ldd.
[x] Inspect the section profile: .text is about 10.4 MB, .eh_frame* about
    1.8 MB combined, .rodata about 1.2 MB, with no anomalous large section.
[x] Record the historical baseline in BINARY_SIZE.md:
    2.22.2 | 1b88628 | x86_64 | 14,997,128 bytes stripped
    SHA-256 b1d4bd91d98614c23b2935458dc1ecdb9ff66e55acec92e3250763a3431cd361.
[x] Do not investigate further with an unstripped binary, nm, a linker map,
    Bloaty, LTO, section garbage collection, or aggressive dependency trimming:
    the first measurements show no anomaly and do not justify optimisation.
[x] Lot 1 decision: 14,997,128 bytes is the release-size baseline. Move on.

Lot 2 — remove opaque folder/embedded test-count assumptions
-------------------------------------------------------------

[x] Audit the current self-test accounting. The observed normal-build baseline
    is 3794 common tests, 15 folder-specific tests, 2 embedded-specific tests,
    and 1 intentionally single-run heavy workers test: 3810 PASS in folder mode
    versus 3796 PASS in embedded mode. These numbers document the current
    baseline; they are not encoded as an invariant.
[x] Explain the former opaque delta: the current +14 folder total is 9 atomic
    --create-exe publication tests + 4 embedded-ZIP limit tests + 1 heavy
    workers node-budget test. The two mode-specific arg tests exist on both
    sides and therefore cancel out in the total delta.
[x] Add explicit common/folder/embedded/single-run accounting to the Lua
    self-test harness instead of comparing a fixed numeric difference.
[x] Make run_tests.sh verify dynamically that every PASS is accounted for,
    common-test counts match across folder/embedded/PATH execution, and
    mode-specific categories never run in the wrong mode.
[x] Add tools/test_selftest_accounting.sh as a structural preflight protecting
    the category model and the absence of a hard-coded folder/embedded delta.
[x] Keep functional behaviour unchanged in this lot.
[x] Do not add the new Lot 3 --create-exe regressions in this lot.
[x] Full maintainer runtime validation is green: 3810 PASS / 0 FAIL in folder
    mode, 3796 PASS / 0 FAIL in embedded mode, 3796 PASS / 0 FAIL via PATH,
    explicit accounting reports 3794 common / 15 folder / 2 embedded / 1
    single-run, and the top-level harness finishes 9/9 modes OK.

